                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Trajectory is a first-person adventure/puzzle sci-fi game, designed for VR, but likewise playable on regular computer systems.  \n \nYou wake up in your space station prison cell and try to find a way to escape (sort of). To do so, it is necessary to accept missions from the station-computer. You are free to decline, but have to face the consequences. Missions are random based and consists of navigating a drone, playing text adventures, completing maintenance tasks, etc.\n\nSounds easy, but it isn’t at all. The developer published a walkthrough guide, which is your best friend. It does not provide all the answers/solutions. You still have to find the exit of each level. (for instance) \nAll takes place in different levels/locations/settings in a zero-gravity environment.\n\nTo discover the multiple endings, it is necessary to complete multiple playthroughs. \n\nI had mixed feelings with regards to level design, graphics, sound, and narration. Sometimes they are decent, sometimes in need of getting used to. (but not bad at all) \n\nGiven the circumstances, one-man developer work, it is a nice little game. 6/10",
